{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1306467-ghosts-becoming-geists-in-two-different-ways","id":1306467,"title":"Ghosts Becoming Geists in Two Different Ways?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-04-21T01:13:54-07:00","id":1306467,"title":"Ghosts Becoming Geists in Two Different Ways?","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">My best friend pointed this out and I thought I'd get clarification from the community. It seems that Ghosts become a Geist by drinking from the Rivers. However, it also seems they can become a Geist by strong emotions. But the latter is only explained in one of the Burdens section, when it should have been explained beforehand. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">\u201c<span style=\"font-family:Arial, sans-serif\">If a ghost drinks deep, he can grow, but not as he is or was. The Underworld itself grows inside him, changing who and what he was into something older, something darker, something further lost. A ghost might become something distinctly other, freed from those last worries, but if he does? He\u2019ll lose as much as he gains, if not more. No one will recognize him, but they\u2019ll fear him all the same. These 'lucky' few become geists, and in doing so, surrender something that they\u2019ll long for as long as they persist.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">And,</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">\u201c<span style=\"font-family:Arial, sans-serif\">While rare, Kindly Sin-Eaters caught up in an accident of extreme emotional attachment at their moment of death may even take on their victim as a geist. So, a Bound who murders her husband and then turns the gun on herself in an elaborate murder-suicide may see the ghost of her lover instantly return to make the Bargain, without either of them ever truly knowing what this choice entails.\u201d</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">If it's true that Ghosts become a Geist by emotional attachment, then what about Resonance?</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">\u201c<span style=\"font-family:Arial, sans-serif\">The Bargain requires death. Not merely the death of the Bound, though of course that\u2019s part of it \u2014 but in order to haul a human being back from the pit, a geist needs a significant source of power, more even than the Essence they feed on. The Bargain draws on <i>resonance, </i>a sort of background radiation created by death. It needn\u2019t be large in scale, but it must be intense. A fatal, three-car pileup could birth a krewe\u2019s worth of Sin-Eaters. A serial killer\u2019s ritual kill room might poison the world for blocks around, enough that a geist can seize hold of it and merge with the old man dying of cancer around the corner. The larger the event, the more powerful the resonance, and Sin-Eaters explode into the world in massive numbers. But where that resonance doesn\u2019t exist, the Bargain can\u2019t be struck.\u201d</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial, sans-serif\">This seems like Geists are well-aware of the Resonance and Bargain is an agreement between a Sin-Eater and a Geist. I think that a person who suddenly died and became a Geist by extreme emotional attachment can't be aware of this to come up with the Bargain since it would take time and he would probably be traumatized by the whole thing. </span></span><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":22337,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/22337-overcastghost","user":"OvercastGhost","date":".  Font 04-21-2019, 04:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/22337-overcastghost","name":"OvercastGhost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar22337_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T04:08:03-07:00","id":1306498,"title":"","content":"Any rank 3 ghost is a geist. The standard way to be a rank 3 is to drink from a river from the underworld, but otherwise exist from mystic convergences, occult rituals, or being the first ghost to form in a graveyard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T10:55:47-07:00","id":1306574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1306467-ghosts-becoming-geists-in-two-different-ways?p=1306498#post1306498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any rank 3 ghost is a geist. The standard way to be a rank 3 is to drink from a river from the underworld, but otherwise exist from mystic convergences, occult rituals, or being the first ghost to form in a graveyard.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! Appreciate the reply.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/22337-overcastghost","name":"OvercastGhost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar22337_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}